course: dictionary
lesson: 1146
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues. «The rider put the bridle on the horse before the ride.» The rider and the horse tell you that a bridle is the straps and metal bit that go on a horse's head.
explain: Bridle can also be an action word. «She bridled at the remark» means she showed sudden offence, often by lifting her head. There is no horse in that sentence, so the context points to the second meaning: a person reacting to something someone said.
explain: Bridle can mean to hold something back, like your temper. «He bridled his anger until the meeting ended.» Try the meaning in the sentence: held back his anger still makes sense, so you know you have chosen the right meaning.
fact: A bridle is the straps, metal bit and reins put on a horse's head to control it.
fact: As a verb, «bridle» can mean to put a bridle on a horse, or to show sudden anger or offence.
fact: «Bridle» can also mean to control or hold back something, such as your temper.
fact: A bridleway, used in the UK, is a path for horses, walkers and bikes.
fact: Many words have several meanings, so always check the context before you decide.
exercise: «The rider put the bridle on the horse before the ride.» In this sentence, what is a bridle? | *The straps, bit and reins put on a horse's head | A path through the woods | A saddle for riding | A kind of horse food
exercise: «She bridled at the remark and turned away.» What does bridled suggest? | She laughed loudly at a joke | *She showed sudden offence | She fed the horse | She went to sleep on the spot
exercise: Which sentence uses bridle to mean hold back? | «The rider bridled the horse in the field» | «The horse's teeth were worn down» | *«He bridled his anger until the meeting ended» | «The bridleway was muddy after the rain»
test: «The bridleway through the forest was closed for the winter.» What is a bridleway? | A rope made for tying horses | *A path for horses, walkers and bikes | A gate into a field | A road for cars only
test: «Mia bridled at her brother's teasing and turned away.» What does bridled mean here? | She put a bridle on her brother | She was happy and laughed | *She showed offence or anger | She was tired and went to bed
exam: «An adult horse has about 36 to 44 teeth, with a gap where the bit of a bridle sits.» In this sentence, what is a bridle? | A kind of tooth | *Straps and a metal bit put on a horse's head | A horse's age | A type of vet
